# Life Admin — Implementation Phases

## Phase 0 — Project Setup

Goal:
Create a stable Next.js 16 foundation.

Tasks:
- Create Next.js TypeScript project.
- Install Tailwind CSS.
- Configure linting/formatting as appropriate.
- Initialize Git.
- Create GitHub repository.
- Create environment variable template.
- Add initial folder structure.

Exit criteria:
- App runs locally.
- Git repository works.
- Basic page renders.

## Phase 1 — Database and Prisma

Tasks:
- Set up PostgreSQL.
- Configure `DATABASE_URL`.
- Initialize Prisma.
- Create User and Document models.
- Add Category enum.
- Add indexes.
- Run initial migration.
- Verify Prisma client.

Exit criteria:
- Database connection works.
- Migration succeeds.
- Prisma queries work.

## Phase 2 — Authentication

Tasks:
- Registration.
- Login.
- Logout.
- Session handling.
- Protected dashboard/documents routes.
- Server-side current-user resolution.

Exit criteria:
- Unauthenticated users cannot access private document data.
- Authenticated user identity is available server-side.

## Phase 3 — Document CRUD API

Tasks:
- Zod create schema.
- Zod update schema.
- POST document.
- GET documents.
- GET document by id.
- PATCH document.
- DELETE document.
- Ownership checks.
- Error responses.

Exit criteria:
- All CRUD operations work.
- Invalid input is rejected.
- Cross-user access is blocked.

## Phase 4 — Documents UI

Tasks:
- Documents page.
- Add document form.
- Edit form.
- Detail/view screen.
- Document cards.
- Desktop table.
- Search.
- Category filter.
- Status filter.
- Sorting.
- Delete confirmation.

Exit criteria:
- Full document management works from UI.

## Phase 5 — Dashboard

Tasks:
- Dashboard header.
- Summary cards.
- Total count.
- Expiring-soon count.
- Expired count.
- Upcoming renewals.
- Quick actions.
- Dashboard API/service if required.

Exit criteria:
- Dashboard accurately reflects database state.

## Phase 6 — UX and Responsive Polish

Tasks:
- Mobile layout.
- Tablet layout.
- Desktop layout.
- Loading skeletons.
- Empty states.
- Error states.
- Form validation messages.
- Accessible focus states.
- Confirmation dialogs.
- Consistent Tailwind design.

Exit criteria:
- Main flows are usable on mobile and desktop.

## Phase 7 — Testing and Security

Tasks:
- Unit tests for expiry calculation.
- Validation tests.
- CRUD integration tests.
- Ownership tests.
- Search/filter tests.
- E2E happy path.
- E2E delete flow.
- Unauthorized access tests.

Exit criteria:
- Critical tests pass.
- Security boundaries are verified.

## Phase 8 — Performance

Tasks:
- Review Server vs Client Components.
- Remove unnecessary client components.
- Optimize database queries.
- Verify indexes.
- Avoid N+1 queries.
- Limit dashboard lists.
- Review bundle and loading behavior.

Exit criteria:
- No obvious performance bottlenecks in core flows.

## Phase 9 — Optional AI

Only after the core application is stable.

Tasks:
- Add AI extraction endpoint/service.
- Define strict extraction schema.
- Validate AI output using Zod.
- Show extracted values for user confirmation.
- Save only validated data.

Exit criteria:
- AI failure does not break normal document creation.
- AI cannot bypass validation/security.

## Phase 10 — Deployment

Tasks:
- Configure production PostgreSQL.
- Configure production environment variables.
- Run migrations.
- Deploy Next.js application.
- Verify authentication.
- Verify CRUD.
- Verify production database.
- Verify responsive UI.
- Verify GitHub repository.
- Add required footer links.

Exit criteria:
- Live application is functional.
- Production smoke tests pass.

## Suggested Development Order

Database
-> Authentication
-> API
-> Documents UI
-> Dashboard
-> UX
-> Testing
-> Performance
-> Optional AI
-> Deployment
